# =============================================================================
# Redis Distributed Security & Rate Limiting (SEC-003)
# =============================================================================
# In multi-instance production environments (e.g. Render, AWS, Kubernetes),
# REDIS_URL is required to share login failure counters, OTP verification limits,
# and API rate limits across all server instances.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
# - Leave REDIS_URL unset/empty. MediArca will automatically use safe in-memory fallback.
#
# PRODUCTION SETUP (Render / Upstash / Redis Cloud):
# 1. Render Managed Redis:
#    - Create a Redis instance in the Render Dashboard (or add `type: redis` to render.yaml).
#    - Copy the "Internal Redis URL" (e.g. redis://red-xxxxxxxxxx:6379).
#    - Add it as the REDIS_URL environment variable in your Web Service dashboard.
# 2. Upstash Redis (Free Serverless):
#    - Create a database at https://upstash.com
#    - Copy the standard Redis connection string (rediss://default:xxxx@xxxx.upstash.io:6379).
#    - Add it as REDIS_URL in your hosting dashboard.
#
# Connection string placeholder:
REDIS_URL="redis://default:[PASSWORD]@[REDIS-HOST]:[PORT]"
# In production, set REQUIRE_REDIS="true" to strictly fail closed if Redis is unavailable.
# Set to "false" to permit local in-memory fallback if Redis is temporarily unreachable.
REQUIRE_REDIS="false"
STRICT_DISTRIBUTED_SECURITY="false"

